    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the direct level rules with a points system, keeping each piece of logic in its natural home.\n\n**`util/MembershipLevels.java`** \u2014 the scoring authority, refactored into two single-responsibility methods:\n- `pointsOf(owner, asOf)` \u2014 starts at 0 and adds `+2` email, `+1` no namesakes (`namesakeCount == 0`), `+2` household of 3+ (new `householdSize` factor), `+3` tenure over 365 days.\n- `levelFor(points)` \u2014 maps points to level: 1 (0-1), 2 (2-3), 3 (4-5), 4 (6+).\n\nEach factor's magnitude and threshold is a named constant, and the household/tenure predicates are private helpers.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 now maps both fields. `membershipPoints(owner)` returns the raw score; `membershipLevel(owner)` derives the level from that same score, so the two fields always agree and share the one computation.\n\n**`rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 computes points once and logs both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipPoints` schema and rewrote the `membershipLevel` description to reflect the points-to-level mapping (this regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field).\n\nThe acceptance test (`membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2` for a fresh owner with email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
