    "probe_text": "I've read the full pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`) and every function class it invokes. Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (applies to the whole endpoint)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` or the request is rejected before any step runs.\n- **Transaction** \u2014 every step below carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all reads and the final write commit as one transaction at the end of the pipeline.\n\n## Validations, in order (each can short-circuit the request)\n\n1. **ValidateNewOwner** \u2014 reads the `@RequestBody` once and republishes it. Rejects with `MissingOwnerFieldsException` if any required field is null/blank: `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and `address` (address is judged blank *after* normalization, so an address that collapses to nothing fails).\n2. **ValidateRegistrationDate** \u2014 `registrationDate` is optional; if supplied it must not be after the server's current date, else `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n3. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 `postcode` optional; if present it must be a 4-digit value valid for the owner's city region, else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n4. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect)* \u2014 rewrites `address` to canonical form (trim/collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE) on the shared request object.\n5. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 converts `telephone` to E.164 and stores it back; rejects with `InvalidTelephoneException` (400) if it can't form valid E.164 or the national-number length is wrong for the country code. *(validation + side-effect)*\n6. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 `email` optional; if present must match the email regex else `InvalidEmailException` (400); a valid one is trimmed and lower-cased back onto the request. *(validation + side-effect)*\n7. **ValidateEmailDomain** \u2014 if email present, its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), else `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n8. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 computes the identity key (normalized telephone + email) and scans all existing owners; an exact whole-key match throws `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n9. **EnsureUniqueHousehold** \u2014 unless the request declares `sharesHousehold`, and only when a postcode is present: computes household id from (last name, postcode) and rejects with `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409) if an existing owner shares it.\n10. **EnsureCityHasCapacity** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, trimmed); if \u2265 50 throws `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n11. **EnsureDailyLimit** \u2014 rolls the effective registration date to a business day and counts owners already registered that day; if \u2265 100 throws `DailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n## Build + side-effects on the entity, in order\n\n12. **BuildOwner** \u2014 maps the (now normalized/validated) request DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`.\n13. **ResolveRegistrationDate** \u2014 sets `registrationDate` to the supplied date (or server date if none), rolled forward off weekends to the next Monday.\n14. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; hash8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over normalized telephone + last name).\n15. **AssignHouseholdId** \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over (normalized last name, postcode).\n16. **AssignIdentityKey** \u2014 sets `identityKey` from the owner's normalized telephone/email (matching the duplicate-detection key).\n17. **CountNamesakes** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of pre-existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n18. **CountHouseholdMembers** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = 1 + pre-existing owners sharing the same `householdId`.\n19. **FlagBulkSignup** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners already registered on the owner's effective business day (soft warning below the hard daily cap).\n20. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`: false for a declared household member or when no postcode; otherwise true (pointing at the first existing owner sharing the household id) if one exists.\n\n## Persist, audit, respond\n\n21. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`, generating the id.\n22. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 logs an `AUDIT` line: owner id, customer code, effective registration date, and derived membership points/level. Leaves the entity unchanged.\n23. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nNote: escalations map through `officefloor/escalation/` handlers (only `MissingOwnerFieldsException` has a project-local handler wired here; the others fall through to Spring's `@RestControllerAdvice`)."
